messages:
maria_support: Escalation from Acme-Widgets — function-calling requests failing schema validation only for OpenAI-compat model variant. Customer report: calls succeed on other models but fail when hitting gpt-4o-openai-compat. Request id: rwd_req_0b9f2c. Account: 98765. They pasted a repro below. Can eng take a look?

maria_support: Repro (sanitized):
```bash
curl -X POST \"https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate\" \\  
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer REDACTED' \\  
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\  
  -d '{
    \"model\": \"gpt-4o-openai-compat\",
    \"messages\": [{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Book a meeting\"}],
    \"functions\": [{
      \"name\": \"book_meeting\",
      \"parameters\": {
        \"type\": \"object\",
        \"properties\": {
          \"date\": {\"type\":\"string\"},
          \"priority\": {\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\": [\"LOW\",\"MEDIUM\",\"HIGH\"]}
        },
        \"required\": [\"date\",\"priority\"]
    } } ],
    \"function_call\": {\"name\": \"book_meeting\"},
    \"temperature\": 0
  }'
```

maria_support: Customer says model returns: function_call.arguments as a JSON *string* in some responses, and when it is an object the priority value is lowercase (\"low\") which our validator rejects. Example of model output they saw: 
```json
{\"id\":\"...\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"choices\":[{\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"function_call\":{\"name\":\"book_meeting\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-03-16T15:00:00Z\\\",\\\"priority\\\":\\\"low\\\"}\"}}],\"usage\":{}}
```

maria_support: Our platform returns a 400 schema_validation_error: 
```
{\"error\":\"schema_validation_error\",\"details\":\"Invalid enum value 'low' for field 'priority' (allowed: [\\\"LOW\\\",\\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\\"HIGH\\\"])\",\"request_id\":\"rwd_req_0b9f2c\"}
```

ingrid_eng: Thanks — I can repro locally with the exact payload. Looks like two separate compatibility issues: 1) arguments sometimes coming back as a JSON-encoded string (we need to parse), and 2) enum casing mismatch. We currently enforce enum equality strictly.

ingrid_eng: Quick questions: which model revision are they on? Any routing policy (dedicated vs hosted) that could change runtime?

maria_support: They say model: gpt-4o-openai-compat@2026-03-10 (hosted). No dedicated routing. Latency seems normal (p95 ~180ms).

alex_dev: For immediate customer workaround, ask them to accept stringified args (if they control client) or to normalize case before sending to Redwood. Example JS snippet to normalize incoming function args:
```js
// Normalize after receiver parses function_call.arguments
let args = typeof fc.arguments === 'string' ? JSON.parse(fc.arguments) : fc.arguments;
args.priority = args.priority && args.priority.toUpperCase();
// then call our internal handler with normalized args
```

ryan_sre: We should also patch our OpenAI-compat normalizer to: 1) auto-parse stringified arguments, and 2) perform case-insensitive enum matching (map to canonical). Will check error rates across tenants.

ryan_sre: Looking at logs: ~12 failures in the last hour for this pattern for multiple customers, all on gpt-4o-openai-compat. Example log snippet: 
```
[1796509987] WARN schema_validation: InvalidEnumValue priority='low' allowed=[LOW,MEDIUM,HIGH] account=98765 request=rwd_req_0b9f2c model=gpt-4o-openai-compat@2026-03-10
```

ingrid_eng: I'll take the change. Plan: add a compat layer step that attempts JSON.parse if args is a string, then run enum canonicalization (lowercase -> mapped uppercase) for any enum typed fields. We'll run a canary on hosted region-us-east-1. Assigning to ENG-ML-5678.

ingrid_eng: Patch outline:
```patch
- if (typeof args === 'string') return error;
+ if (typeof args === 'string') args = safeJsonParse(args);
+ // enum normalizer
+ for (const field of schema.enumFields) {
+   if (typeof args[field] === 'string') args[field] = args[field].toUpperCase();
+ }
```

deployment-bot: Created internal issue ENG-ML-5678: \"OpenAI-compat: parse stringified function_call.arguments and canonicalize enum casing\" — https://redwood.internal/issue/ENG-ML-5678 (priority: high)

maria_support: I'll send Acme-Widgets the quick JS workaround and let them know we're patching on our side; will give ETA once canary is green.

alex_dev: Also add a regression test to our OpenAI-compat suite: case-insensitive enum and stringified-arguments combos.

ryan_sre: FYI — if we push mapping we should monitor for accidental collisions (e.g., different enum families). Suggest whitelist of schema fields to normalise, not global.

maria_support: Thanks all — I'll follow up in ticket and post update here when customer confirms. :thumbsup:
